        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 151 adds support for the CSS color <code class=\"notranslate\">alpha()</code> function: see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5070160203481088\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5070160203481088</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is already documented, but the support data is missing: <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/color_value/alpha\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/color_value/alpha</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds the necessary data.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Through testing, I also saw evidence of this working in Firefox preview (Nightly).</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29997",
            "title": "Chrome 151 CSS alpha() function",
            "date_modified": "2026-07-08T09:13:02.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-07-07T11:40:19.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The <a href=\"https://collector.openwebdocs.org/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://collector.openwebdocs.org/</a> project (v10.20.2) found new features shipping in Chromium 151 beta which was released on Friday. Currently, the collector covers about 90% of BCD, so the following list might not be exhaustive. Also, if a feature is in Canary/behind flags, it is not considered here.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">With this PR, BCD will consider the following 18 features as shipping in Chromium 151 (<strong>bold</strong> features are new keys in BCD).</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>api.AnimationEvent.animation</li>\n<li>api.Blob.textStream</li>\n<li><strong>api.PerformanceEntry.navigationId</strong></li>\n<li>api.Request.textStream</li>\n<li>api.Response.textStream</li>\n<li>api.SpeechRecognition.unspokenPunctuation</li>\n<li>api.TransitionEvent.animation</li>\n<li>api.WebTransportDatagramDuplexStream.incomingMaxBufferedDatagrams</li>\n<li>api.WebTransportDatagramDuplexStream.outgoingMaxBufferedDatagrams</li>\n<li><strong>api.WheelEvent.momentum</strong></li>\n<li>css.properties.position-anchor.normal</li>\n<li>css.properties.ruby-overhang</li>\n<li>css.properties.ruby-overhang.auto</li>\n<li><strong>css.properties.ruby-overhang.spaces</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Updated in different PRs:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>api.HTMLElement.headingOffset</li>\n<li>api.HTMLElement.headingReset</li>\n<li>html.global_attributes.headingoffset</li>\n<li>html.global_attributes.headingreset</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See also <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/chrome-151-beta\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/chrome-151-beta</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29988",
            "title": "Updates for Chrome 151 beta",
            "date_modified": "2026-07-07T10:00:59.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-07-06T16:07:35.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Elchi3",
                "url": "https://github.com/Elchi3"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Update Chromium to full support for WebGPU in version 144+. No more partial as it now also ships on Linux. The remark that Linux support is Intel Gen12+ GPUs only, is mentioned in a note still but without partial_implementation: true.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Linux support enabled in <a href=\"https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/0e492e6f38a84951f18d3cb3168b8ed091862738\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/0e492e6f38a84951f18d3cb3168b8ed091862738</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-144#webgpu_on_linux\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-144#webgpu_on_linux</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #28451.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3622558757\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28451\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28451/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28451\">#28451</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See also</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2252751022\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/915\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/915/hovercard?comment_id=4851590415&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/915#issuecomment-4851590415\">web-platform-dx/web-features#915 (comment)</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3231699289\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/developer-signals/issues/202\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/web-platform-dx/developer-signals/issues/202/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/developer-signals/issues/202\">web-platform-dx/developer-signals#202</a></li>\n</ul>",
